# 🧠 2026 MODERN NFS + AUTOFs COMMAND CHEATSHEET

---

# 🟢 PART 1 — NFS SERVER (RHEL 9 / UBUNTU 24.04)

---

## 📌 Install NFS SERVER (SERVER SIDE)

```bash
sudo dnf install -y nfs-utils
```

👉 Installs NFS server tools (RHEL)

```bash
sudo apt install -y nfs-kernel-server
```

👉 Installs NFS server daemon (Ubuntu)

---

## 📌 Enable NFS SERVICE (SERVER SIDE)

```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now nfs-server
```

👉 Starts NFS server and enables auto-start

---

## 📌 Create EXPORT DIRECTORY (SERVER SIDE)

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /srv/nfs/share
```

👉 Creates shared folder

```bash
sudo chmod 755 /srv/nfs/share
```

👉 Sets safe permissions

---

## 📌 Configure EXPORTS (SERVER SIDE)

```bash
sudo nano /etc/exports
```

```bash
/srv/nfs/share 192.168.1.0/24(rw,sync,root_squash,no_subtree_check)
```

👉 Defines allowed client network + permissions

---

## 📌 APPLY EXPORTS (SERVER SIDE)

```bash
sudo exportfs -rav
```

👉 Activates export configuration

```bash
sudo exportfs -v
```

👉 Shows active exports

---

## 📌 FIREWALL OPEN (SERVER SIDE)

```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-service=nfs
sudo firewall-cmd --reload
```

👉 Opens NFS access (RHEL)

```bash
sudo ufw allow 2049/tcp
```

👉 Opens NFS port (Ubuntu)

---

## 📌 VERIFY SERVER (SERVER SIDE)

```bash
ss -tulpn | grep 2049
```

👉 Confirms NFS is running

```bash
exportfs -v
```

👉 Checks exports

---

# 🟡 PART 2 — NFS CLIENT (RHEL / UBUNTU)

---

## 📌 Install CLIENT PACKAGES (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo dnf install -y nfs-utils
```

👉 RHEL client tools

```bash
sudo apt install -y nfs-common
```

👉 Ubuntu client tools

---

## 📌 Create MOUNT POINT (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo mkdir -p /mnt/nfs
```

👉 Folder where NFS will mount

---

## 📌 MANUAL MOUNT TEST (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo mount -t nfs4 server_ip:/srv/nfs/share /mnt/nfs
```

👉 Temporary mount test

---

## 📌 VERIFY MOUNT (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
df -h | grep nfs
```

👉 Shows mounted filesystem

```bash
nfsstat -m
```

👉 Displays NFS mount details

---

## 📌 TEST WRITE (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
touch /mnt/nfs/testfile
```

👉 Checks read/write access

---

# 🟢 PART 3 — MODERN SYSTEMD AUTOMOUNT (BEST PRACTICE)

---

## 📌 FSTAB ENTRY (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo nano /etc/fstab
```

```bash
server_ip:/srv/nfs/share /mnt/nfs nfs4 defaults,_netdev,nofail,x-systemd.automount,x-systemd.idle-timeout=600 0 0
```

👉 Auto-mount on access (no boot hang)

---

## 📌 APPLY FSTAB (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo mount -a
```

👉 Activates systemd automount

---

# 🟡 PART 4 — AUTOFs (ENTERPRISE DYNAMIC MOUNT)

---

## 📌 INSTALL AUTOFs (CLIENT SIDE ONLY)

```bash
sudo dnf install -y autofs
```

👉 RHEL autofs install

```bash
sudo apt install -y autofs
```

👉 Ubuntu autofs install

---

## 📌 ENABLE AUTOFs (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo systemctl enable --now autofs
```

👉 Starts autofs service

---

## 📌 MASTER CONFIG (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo nano /etc/auto.master
```

```bash
/mnt/nfs /etc/auto.nfs --timeout=300 --ghost
```

👉 Defines auto-mount root + timeout

---

## 📌 MAP FILE (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo nano /etc/auto.nfs
```

```bash
share -fstype=nfs4 server_ip:/srv/nfs/share
```

👉 Defines actual NFS mount

---

## 📌 RESTART AUTOFs (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
sudo systemctl restart autofs
```

👉 Applies config

---

## 📌 TEST AUTOFs (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
ls /mnt/nfs/share
```

👉 Triggers automatic mount

---

## 📌 VERIFY AUTOFs (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
mount | grep nfs
```

👉 Confirms active mount

---

## 📌 TROUBLESHOOT AUTOFs (CLIENT SIDE)

```bash
journalctl -u autofs -f
```

👉 Live logs for debugging

---

